The Vulnerability You Are Looking For: Sometimes developers create sensitive, secret pages (like an internal employee login, a database viewer, or a control panel) and simply assume: "Nobody will find this because there is no link to it on the home page."

The Reality: Attackers don't rely on clicking links. They guess common URL paths directly into the browser. Finding hidden administrative areas this way is a fundamental reconnaissance technique called Directory Brute-Forcing or Content Discovery.

The Rules of the Exercise
You have a base URL: [http://www.onlineshop.thm/](http://www.onlineshop.thm/)

You have a checklist of 5 common paths to append to the end:

/sitemap

/mail

/register

/login

/admin

You test them one by one in the browser address bar.
